# std/stack-merge-to-master (design/stack-publish.md, "stack-merge-to-master"):
# an ordinary worker (design/tool-contract.md). It holds no token: every
# GitHub call goes through its neighbour `DEEP-DEPS/github`, the one image the
# github-token is granted to.
HELP=<<END
Merge the pull requests of the published stack `root` (such as sources/repo; std/GIT.md, "Merging a stack"), bottom to top, each squashed onto the trunk with its NN-<name>.pr.md as the commit message: the first line plus the PR number as the title, the rest as the body, whatever the repository's default squash message is. Before anything is merged, every layer to merge must have an open pull request whose head is the layer's commit (else: stack-sync, stack-publish first), and CI on each of those heads must be passing: a failing or unfinished check refuses the whole merge unless force is true, and the refusal lists every check of the layers that are not passing. With wait-for-ci-min it first waits for unfinished CI, until a check fails or none is pending, for at most that many minutes. The PRs are then merged one at a time with GitHub's asynchronous merge, each once GitHub has pointed it at the trunk (which GitHub does itself for a linked stack after the PR below merges). A merge that fails stops there: the layers below are merged, the ones above are not touched, and running again carries on. The result is one line per layer (branch, PR, checks, outcome). Afterwards run stack-sync with remove-merged=true. Does not push, delete branches or wait for CI on the branches GitHub rebases.
@param [up-to] The top layer to merge, by name (02-tests), number (02) or branch name (tests); the layers below it merge too. Default: every described layer.
@param [branch-prefix] Text put before every branch name, the same value given to stack-publish.
@param [repository] HTTPS repository URL, without credentials. Default: the repository 00-base was imported from.
@param [trunk] The branch the stack merges into. Default: the branch 00-base was imported from, or the remote's default branch.
@param [force] true to merge although CI is failing or has not finished on some layer.
@param [wait-for-ci-min] Minutes to wait for CI on the layers' heads to settle before deciding, reading every 15 seconds. Default 0, read once.
@param [dry-run] true to read the pull requests and their checks and report what would be merged, merging nothing.
@root
@request-id
END
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/go --worker1:@=worker.go --github:@=DEEP-DEPS/github --help=$HELP
